* Zama KMS
** Threshold model
*** n = 13 parties, t = 4, t < n/3
*** Maliciously secure, robust MPC
*** Noah's Ark: noise flooding
*** 128-bit security, p-fail 2^-128
*** sk never exists in one place
** Operations (gRPC)
*** Preprocessing: hours, Gateway-driven
*** KeyGen: TFHE key set, shares per party
*** CrsGen: powers-of-tau for ZKPoK
*** PublicDecrypt: seconds, signed plaintext
*** UserDecrypt: signcrypted shares, 2t+1
*** NewMpcEpoch: resharing, party rotation
*** Signing schemes: ECDSA, Ed25519, ML-DSA
** Node anatomy
*** kms-server: core (50100, localhost) + threshold (50001)
*** Connector: listener, worker (ACL check), tx sender
*** Private vault, public Keychain DA, backup vault
*** Keychain: AWS KMS or custodian shares
*** Identity: ECDSA key + root signing seed
*** Boot-time storage verification
** Networking and enclaves
*** mTLS, self-signed CA per party, CN checked per message
*** PrivateLink between parties
*** Nitro Enclave, 48 CPU / 96 GiB
*** Attested TLS, PCR allowlist
** Backup and recovery
*** Automatic encrypted backups
*** RestoreFromBackup (AWS KMS)
*** Custodians, BIP39 seed phrases, quorum
*** Fixed restore order, recovery mode
** Deployment of one party
*** Terraform: EKS, S3, IAM/IRSA, KMS key
*** kms-core Helm chart, StatefulSet
*** kms-gen-keys, kms-init (PRSS once)
*** Key generation via the Gateway
*** Ports: 50100 never exposed, 50001 peers, 9646 metrics
@endmindmap
